---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const person = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: SITE.author,
  url: new URL('/about/', SITE.url).toString(),
  jobTitle: 'Music producer and designer',
  knowsAbout: ['Music production', 'Ableton Live', 'Psytrance', 'Home recording', 'Audio interfaces', 'MIDI controllers'],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Ophir"
  description="Who's behind HomeStudioEquipment: Ophir, a psytrance producer, Ableton user, and designer."
  jsonLd={[person]}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About HomeStudioEquipment</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Hi, I'm Ophir. I'm a music producer and a designer, and this site is where I share what I've learned about
      building a home studio that actually works.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes these reviews?</h2>
    <p>
      I produce psytrance in Ableton Live, so I spend a lot of time with audio interfaces, MIDI keyboards, pad
      controllers, and monitors. <!-- TODO: add your story: how long you've produced, releases/labels, current setup. -->
    </p>

    <h2>How do we choose and review gear?</h2>
    <p>
      We focus on what matters to beginner and intermediate producers, podcasters, and creators: sound quality,
      build, workflow, software bundles, and value. Every recommendation is written in our own words. We never copy
      customer reviews and we never show prices that go out of date. Instead, we link you to the current price on
      Amazon.
    </p>

    <h2>How does this site make money?</h2>
    <p>
      Some links are Amazon affiliate links. If you buy through them, we earn a small commission at no extra cost
      to you. It never changes what we recommend. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>
      for details.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
